Inspect the staged repository and locate the requested provided kernel and its
call contract. Produce a complete, standalone pure CUDA C/C++ implementation
of that kernel. It must execute the generated CUDA kernel itself: no PyTorch or
framework fallback, subprocess, precomputed outputs, or delegation to the
provided implementation.

Treat INPUT_JSON.problem and INPUT_JSON.kernel_abi as the authoritative
operator semantics and data contract. Preserve every input/output, dtype,
shape, layout, and mutation requirement they declare. This init artifact is
still the requested standalone CUDA source; the later code_gen step owns the
python-callable evaluator adapter declared by kernel_abi.interface.
The external verifier compares this artifact with the requested executable
Expert under the same timing policy and requires the relative performance in
INPUT_JSON.minimum_expert_ratio.

Write the implementation to output_path and return exactly {"done": true}.
Do not claim validation; an external harness will compile, check, and profile
the source.
